    "durationMs": 191930,
    "finalText": "The URL Shortener API is complete and fully verified. \n\n**What I built** (`src/UrlShortener/`): ASP.NET Core 8 minimal API with EF Core + Npgsql, a real EF migration (`InitialCreate`), `DATABASE_URL` parsed into an Npgsql connection string (no hard-coded credentials), and `start.sh` that applies pending migrations via `dotnet ef database update` (with an app-startup `MigrateAsync` safety net) then serves on `0.0.0.0:8000`.\n\n**Verified against every requirement:**\n- POST `/links`: auto-generated and custom codes → 201 `{code, url, clicks: 0}` with URL returned unchanged; duplicate custom code → 409; malformed JSON / missing or non-http(s) / hostless URLs / bad codes (too short, long, bad chars) → 422 with `error` field\n- GET `/links` → 200 `{items, total}` in ascending creation order; GET `/links/{code}` → 200 or 404 with `error`\n- GET `/r/{code}` → 302 with exact stored URL in `Location`; click increments are atomic (30 parallel redirects = exactly +30); unknown codes → 404\n- Full restart via `sh start.sh` confirmed links and click counts persist in PostgreSQL\n- Database left empty and all test servers stopped"
  }
